id: pm-mrh0ae
title: "HTTP-native MCP transport convergence: one Streamable HTTP contract spans remote servers and local stdio deployment without semantic forks"
description: "Unify local and remote MCP deployment around the same HTTP-native request routing, metadata, streaming, cancellation, security, and error semantics while retaining stdio only as a transport carrier. The public SDK must expose one conformance surface rather than parallel local and remote implementations."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: "area:mcp","area:sdk",http-native,local-server,stdio,streamable-http,transport
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:17.691Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:58:31.574Z"
deadline: "2027-06-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: Local stdio and remote HTTP use the same request and response semantics and protocol-era codecs; method name parameter and trace headers have one validation contract; process lifecycle backpressure cancellation timeout and disconnect behavior are equivalent; adapters never reimplement SDK policy; proxy origin host header and injection boundaries have negative controls; conformance runs the same scenario matrix through both carriers; migration preserves bounded legacy compatibility without sessions or hidden connection state
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: high
confidence: medium
